Chapter: BundledAgentHeapProbe
  cites Works chapter AgentBundle

 The same chain as `bundled-agent`, with the heap read on either side of it.

 `__heap-save` answers the bump allocator's current position, so the difference
 across the verdict is exactly what verifying the bundle consumed and did not
 give back. That number is the whole claim: it must not grow with the size of
 the model. The harness runs this against two images whose models differ by a
 factor of eight hundred and compares.

 The label is printed rather than the full report because the report builds
 Text, and Text allocated before the second reading would be counted as part of
 the verification. The reading is taken first for the same reason.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  bahp-report : Integer, AgentBundleVerdict -> [Console] Nothing
  bahp-report (before) (v) =
    let after = __heap-save
    in act
      print-line-uni (bundle-verdict-label v)
      print-line-uni ("heap " & show (after - before))
    end

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    let before = __heap-save
    in act
      v <- bundled-agent-verdict
      bahp-report before v
    end
  end
